Steps:
[GQL-ENDPOINT /graphql/sales-rep]
[AUTH role=SALES_REP]
[GQL-OP cart_rules]
query { salesRepCartFilterRules(storeId: "{{store}}", cultureName: "{{culture}}") { __typename } }
[GQL-EXEC cart_rules]
[GQL-OP order_filter_rules]
query { salesRepOrderFilterRules(storeId: "{{store}}", cultureName: "{{culture}}") { __typename } }
[GQL-EXEC order_filter_rules]
[GQL-OP order_sort_rules]
query { salesRepOrderSortRules(storeId: "{{store}}", cultureName: "{{culture}}") { __typename } }
[GQL-EXEC order_sort_rules]
[GQL-OP customer_filter_rules]
query { salesRepCustomerFilterRules(storeId: "{{store}}", cultureName: "{{culture}}") { __typename } }
[GQL-EXEC customer_filter_rules]
[GQL-OP customer_sort_rules]
query { salesRepCustomerSortRules(storeId: "{{store}}", cultureName: "{{culture}}") { __typename } }
[GQL-EXEC customer_sort_rules]
[GQL-OP topseller_filter_rules]
query { salesRepTopSellerFilterRules(storeId: "{{store}}", cultureName: "{{culture}}") { __typename } }
[GQL-EXEC topseller_filter_rules]
[GQL-OP topseller_sort_rules]
query { salesRepTopSellerSortRules(storeId: "{{store}}", cultureName: "{{culture}}") { __typename } }
[GQL-EXEC topseller_sort_rules]

Assertions:
[ERRORS label=cart_rules] errors[] empty {SPEC}
[ERRORS label=order_filter_rules] errors[] empty {SPEC}
[ERRORS label=order_sort_rules] errors[] empty {SPEC}
[ERRORS label=customer_filter_rules] errors[] empty {SPEC}
[ERRORS label=customer_sort_rules] errors[] empty {SPEC}
[ERRORS label=topseller_filter_rules] errors[] empty {SPEC}
[ERRORS label=topseller_sort_rules] errors[] empty {SPEC}

[DOM] verify whether the Sales Rep workspace tile/menu entry is visible at all for an admin lacking the role VCST-5293 introduces {HYPOTHESIS}
[DOM] verify whether, if the tile IS visible and clicked, the embedded app blocks with a permission-denied state rather than rendering live rep/org data {HYPOTHESIS}
[GRID] verify whether any grid data (Sales Reps / Organizations counts) is visible to this restricted admin if the app does render {HYPOTHESIS}

[DOM] verify whether the "My customers" hub link is visible in the left rail for SR_REP_NOCUSTOMERS (global sales-rep:access role, zero org memberships) {HYPOTHESIS}
[NAV] IF the link was clicked THEN record the resulting URL (expected redirect target per 089 SR-FE-013 is /account/dashboard) {OBSERVED}
[STATE] verify whether the resulting state is a jarring unexplained redirect (VCST-5494's reported symptom) vs a graceful in-place empty/no-access message (a candidate fix direction) {HYPOTHESIS}

[NAV] verify the resulting URL for the Sales Rep hub Dashboard page (record it — do not assume a literal path) {HYPOTHESIS}
[DOM] verify whether a distinct Dashboard heading/container element renders that is not the My Customers table already covered by 089 (e.g. a summary-statistics widget region or recent-activity list element) {HYPOTHESIS}
[STATE] verify whether the Dashboard is the DEFAULT landing when clicking the hub section itself (mirrors the Admin embedded app's default-Dashboard-tab behavior confirmed in 092 SR-ADM-001) {HYPOTHESIS}
